# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. Anything committed is world-readable forever, and
# git history keeps it after a later deletion.
#
# The rubric workbooks in rubrics/source/ ARE committed deliberately — they are
# a blank review template with no personal data. Course exports are NOT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Working data. Root is configurable as SIGHTLINE_DATA_DIR (default ./data).
# Course exports, caches, run state and generated reports all live under it and
# none of it is ever committed. Exports carry instructor-authored content, page
# text naming real people, and unpublished drafts.
data/
*.imscc

# Secrets. The Canvas base URL is institution-identifying and is treated as a
# secret in this repo, not just the token.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.token
config.local.*
instance/

# Local scratch — an escape hatch for anything that must stay off the remote.
private/

# Runtime
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# examples/ is committed on purpose — it is the synthetic sample course and a
# sample report, so a new user sees the shape of both without a Canvas token.
!examples/
